# s5_keybuf_tight
#
# donor      this line's s2/s3/s4, BumbleBee b4_slice_budget_64m. Claims the slack s3 kept on a
#            reason later found wrong.
# basis      s4_dealerbuf_measured host peak, rank-1 row (dealer buffers at 64 MiB after s4):
#              keyBuf      18 GiB, of which 16.83 GiB written    <- this step
#              llamaBuf1   64 MiB   sized by s4
#              dummyBuf1   64 MiB   sized by s4
#            1.17 GiB unwritten but resident (cudaHostRegister; s3, s4 predicted to 0.12%, 0.11%).
# backstop   SIGMAKeygen::close() ends with
#                assert(keySize < keyBufSize);
#            live in the binary (NDEBUG not defined); close() runs before the online phase (sigma.cu:
#            sigmaKeygen->close(), then new SIGMA<u64>(...)). Over-tight buffer: heap corruption, then
#            abort; no plausible wrong number. Correction carried in s3's and s4's levers.env.
# need       deterministic (network shape and operation sequence, MANIFEST.md; not PRNG values):
#              s2_commbuf_measured    keybuf_used=18075947008
#              s3_keybuf_measured     keybuf_used=18075947008
#              s4_dealerbuf_measured  keybuf_used=18075947008
#              s5_keybuf_tight        keybuf_used=18075947008    (this run, fourth identical observation)
#
# impl_lever: patches/patch_keybuf_tight.py
# The one lever of this step.
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: main
# cost_class: free
#
# name       `main` = grouped-table name, as in s3 and s4.
# lever      keyBufSz 18 * OneGB -> 17 * OneGB, bert-base branch only.
#              17 GiB = 18,253,611,008 B against 18,075,947,008 B needed
#              margin 177,664,000 B = 169 MB = 0.98%, buffer now 99.03% full
# free       oversized reservation; pinning 17 GiB is less work than 18.
# measured   n=1 (replicates: 1, MANIFEST), job 46145284:
#              peak host   20,101,276 -> 19,052,324 kB   -1,048,952 kB   -5.22%
#              runtime             27 s wall
#              gate        T1s, bit-identical to s4
#              marker      SNNI_BUF|keybuf_used=18075947008|keybuf_alloc=18253611008
#            predicted 1,048,576 kB, measured 1,048,952 kB (0.036%).
# build      build_step_binary.sbatch greps the binary for the assert string (grep -a; `strings` is
#            absent on compute nodes after module purge) and fails without it.
# falsifier  saving far below 1 GiB, assert abort, or moved gate; none occurred.
